course: dictionary
lesson: 10264
title: Toot: a sound, a boast, and a joke
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: Toot has more than one meaning, so context tells you which one is meant. Its most common meaning is a short, high sound made by a horn or whistle. «The driver gave a toot to warn the cyclist.» The clue is the warning: a toot is a sound that tells people to be careful.
explain: Look at the words around it. «The trumpeters are tooting and the soldiers are saluting» describes a loud, noisy scene, so toot here means to sound out with a horn or trumpet. Picture a concert hall where everyone is tooting at once while the orchestra tunes up. The noise stops when the conductor walks on.
explain: Toot also has a figure-of-speech meaning. In the US, «toot your own horn» means to boast about yourself. In the UK people say «blow your own trumpet». Ask: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: To toot is to make a short, high sound with a horn or whistle.
fact: A toot is one such short sound, as in «a toot on the horn».
fact: «Toot your own horn» (US) means to boast about yourself; in the UK, people say «blow your own trumpet».
fact: In stories, «the train tooted as it left the station», and the word copies the sound it makes.
fact: Children sometimes use «toot» as a silly, polite word for passing wind (fart). It is a jokey word, so use it only when it fits the situation.
exercise: «The driver gave a short toot to warn the cyclist.» What does toot mean here? | A bright light | *A short, high sound from a horn | A long song sung by a choir | A bump into a wall
exercise: Sam says «toot your own horn» means to play a trumpet in the school band. What does it really mean? | To practise music at home | *To boast about yourself | To tell someone the time | To wave to your friends
exercise: Copy the word from «The trumpeters are tooting and the soldiers are saluting» that means to sound a horn or trumpet. | trumpeters | soldiers | *tooting | saluting
test: «The train tooted as it left the station.» What does toot mean here? | Slow movement on the rails | A shout to stop | A sad goodbye song | *A short, high whistle or horn sound
test: Which phrase means the same as «blow your own trumpet»? | To forget your lines | *To boast about yourself | To play a tune badly | To shout in a park
exam: A child says «toot» is a silly, polite word. In which meaning is that true? | The sound of a car horn | *A jokey word for passing wind | A quiet whisper | A boast about yourself
